				<div id="essay">
					<h2>A winner on the ice&#8212;and in life</h2>
					<p>When Emily was nine years old, she discovered her true passion was figure skating. She began private lessons and created a vision for what her skating goals would be. </p>
					<p class="pullquote">Emily works hard yet never forgets to have fun and enjoy her passion.</p>
					<p>Emily is very committed to figure skating not only as a solo performer but also as a member of the Theatre on Ice (TOI) team. This is the third year Emily has skated for the TOI team, and she is very attentive to the younger members by helping them with their parts in the show.  She encourages them to work hard&#8212;and have fun.</p>
					<p>The team routinely holds fund-raisers where Emily is always an essential contributor, working hard at all of the events&#8212;even when she is not competing. Emily has contributed by doing everything from baking cupcakes to selling lemonade at football games.</p>
					<p>Emily works closely with her coaches and family to set realistic goals. This past summer, Emily progressed three levels&#8212;all due to her hard work and determination. Last June, when Emily entered a competition, she requested she be moved up past her given level. She explained to her coach that she wanted to be challenged.</p>
					<p class="last">One of Emily&#8217;s strongest characteristics is her perseverance. One afternoon Emily stayed in one spot on the ice for 50 minutes and worked on a new spin. In those 50 minutes she improved little by little. Her spin was not perfect when she left that day, but on her next visit to the ice park, Emily was back on the ice working on that spin. Even when many would become discouraged and give up, Emily keeps her head held high and continues to work even harder.  She never forgets to have fun and enjoy her passion.</p>
				</div>
